#### Problem 9: Cost Optimization — $180K/Month Cloud Bill to $45K

**Scenario you describe:**
> "The team was running everything on Large All-Purpose clusters that stayed up 24/7. 8 analysts sharing 3 clusters. Monthly DBU cost: $180K. CTO asked me to cut it by 60% without impacting productivity."

**Solution — Compute Right-Sizing:**

| Change | Before | After | Savings |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **SQL workloads → Serverless SQL Warehouse** | Large all-purpose cluster 24/7 | Small serverless WH, auto-stops in 10 min | 70% (pay only when querying) |
| **Nightly ETL → Job Clusters** | Ran on always-on cluster | Dedicated job cluster, terminates after completion | 60% (runs 2 hours, not 24) |
| **Dev/test → X-Small clusters with auto-stop** | Large cluster for development | X-Small with 15-min auto-stop | 80% |
| **Caching layer** | Every dashboard query hit raw tables | Materialized views for top 10 dashboards | 40% fewer queries |
| **Spot instances for non-critical** | All on-demand | Job clusters use spot/preemptible workers | 30% per cluster |

**Architecture:**

| Workload Type | Compute | Size | Auto-Stop | Who |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Ad-hoc SQL | Serverless SQL WH | Small (auto-scales) | 10 min | Analysts |
| Dashboard serving | Serverless SQL WH | Medium (shared) | 20 min | BI consumers |
| ETL pipelines | Job Clusters | Medium + spot workers | On completion | Scheduled |
| ML training | All-Purpose (ML Runtime) | GPU-enabled | 30 min | Data scientists |
| Dev notebooks | Serverless SQL WH | Small | 10 min | Engineers |

**What makes this principal-level:**
- You didn't just downsize — you **re-architected compute allocation** by workload type
- You built a **cost attribution dashboard** by team/user using `system.billing.usage` — made costs visible
- You introduced **tagging policies**: every cluster must have `team`, `project`, `environment` tags for chargeback
- You negotiated **reserved capacity** for the base workload (further 20% discount on predictable portion)

