### PART D: Interview Answer Framework (STAR+)

Use this structure for every answer:

| Element | What to Say | Time |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **S - Situation** | Set the scene: team size, data volume, business impact | 15 sec |
| **T - Task** | What was your specific responsibility | 10 sec |
| **A - Action** | Technical details: what you did, tools used, tradeoffs evaluated | 45 sec |
| **R - Result** | Quantified impact: time saved, cost reduced, SLA met | 15 sec |
| **+ Scale** | How you made it reusable: framework, monitoring, documentation, team enablement | 15 sec |

> **Principal-level differentiator**: Junior engineers fix the bug. Senior engineers fix the class of bugs. **Principal engineers design systems where that class of bugs cannot occur.**
